course: dictionary
lesson: 6638
title: New Year in spring
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Not every country starts its new year in January. Some start in spring and some in autumn. «New Year can be in winter, spring or autumn» shows that the date depends on the place and its traditions.
explain: Nowruz is a proper noun, so it begins with a capital letter. It is the Persian New Year, a spring festival that comes on the spring equinox, around 20 or 21 March. The equinox is the time when day and night are about equal in length.
explain: Use context to understand new words. «Nowruz, the Persian New Year, comes on the first day of spring» tells you that Nowruz is a new year and that it happens in spring. The word Persian tells you the festival belongs to Persian culture.
fact: Nowruz means the Persian New Year, and it is a spring festival.
fact: Nowruz comes on the spring equinox, around 20 or 21 March.
fact: Nowruz is celebrated in Iran, Afghanistan, Central Asia and Azerbaijan, and by Kurds and others.
fact: Families celebrate Nowruz by cleaning the house and visiting relatives.
fact: A special table called haft-sin is set for Nowruz.
exercise: What is Nowruz? | A Scottish winter sport | *The Persian New Year, a spring festival | A type of Ethiopian food | A summer holiday at the seaside
exercise: «Nowruz comes on the first day of spring» gives roughly which date? | 1 January | 25 December | *20 or 21 March | 31 October
exercise: Which country celebrates Nowruz? | *Iran | Canada | Brazil | Japan
test: Why is Nowruz called a spring festival? | Because it is held in the middle of winter | Because it is held on a summer holiday | *Because it comes on the first day of spring | Because it is held in the autumn
test: What does the word Persian in «the Persian New Year» tell you? | The festival is in the middle of winter | Persian is the name of a month | *The festival belongs to Persian culture | The festival is held only in Scotland
exam: «Ethiopian New Year in September» tells us that Ethiopian New Year comes in which month? | December | *September | March | January
